{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1416764-need-help-with-designing-manse-defenses","id":1416764,"title":"Need Help With Designing Manse Defenses","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-10-04T14:17:00-07:00","id":1416764,"title":"Need Help With Designing Manse Defenses","content":"So next session I'm going to have the PCs attack a couple of manses: The Burning Breath of Heseish and The House of Black Waters.<br /> <br /> I'm trying to work about appropriate levels of resistance for these targets.<br /> <br /> I figure that there might well be an entire Sworn Kingship guarding the Breath. It's a fire aspected manse which (in my game and previous editions) sits reasonably close to the Imperial City and is held by House Cathak. It's supposed to be impossible for anyone by Fire Aspected Dragon-Blooded to endure it comfortably, so I'm figuring heat-based environmental penalities and hazards. Maybe a Guarda Bird drawn to the Essence of the place (maybe two Guarda Birds, courting each other with a mind toward self immolation). The manse itself is a giant dragon statue filled with super-heated volcanic air, and ringed by a compound of buildings on top of a hill -- so I'm thinking clear lines of sight, not two many &quot;traps&quot;, flying enemies, more or less a straight fight in a hostile environment. Easy, done, move on.<br /> <br /> The House of Black Waters is the public home of House Iselsi. It's also where they keep the details of their Vendetta against the Realm. I figure it's got to be pretty well defended. If it's the public face of House Iselsi, I figure there's got to be, what, a ~8 Young Dynast level Dragon-Blooded, ~3 Shikari level, 2 Experienced Dragon-Blooded and a Berit level House Elder (will probably reskin the QCs out of Heirs so it's not quite so generic as that). Plus bound demons. And it's a Water Aspected manse. Folks on Discord have suggested it be filled with traps... but I'm struggling to see how that plays out in play.<br /> <br /> For example, folks are saying use &quot;Saw&quot; as inspiration. But the PCs are attacking the manse. They've not been kidnapped and placed inside the manse. The manse that is the public facing headquarters of House Iselsi. I'm not sure how much of Saw is useable. It's a great aestic, I just don't know how I practically translate it into Exalted. Someone suggested a room where they have to torture someone to pass through to the next room, but the correct torture tools are hidden in room and they have to find them then work out what the correct method of torture is... I'm not even sure how I'd reduce that to a dice roll... or how I'd frame that scene narratively (like, unless they watch a creepy video of a doll on a tricycle explaining to them that they need to torture someone, how do you even convey that this is what they have to do by the set up of the room).<br /> <br /> Poison on papers, doorknobs etc. all seems pretty straightforward. Rolls to lockpick doors. Easy basic dungeon stuff. But it seems kinda... boring to me. &quot;You disturb the poison on the desk, and inhale the dust roll [Stamina+Resistance] against Curea.&quot; I don't want stuff which is &quot;roll this dice pool and instantly win&quot;: if I'm going to think up puzzles and traps, then I want the players (not the characters) to have to think up how they're going to get past them. Straightforward stuff like &quot;roll against this poison&quot; is great as an entree (roll against poison, now you're poisoned you have to fight this demon). But I need main courses: I'm thinking seven back-to-back challenges - two noncombat, one combat, three noncombat, one boss combat.<br /> <br /> One thing I really like is a Jonathan Strange &amp; Mr Norrell style maze, where the manse rearranges itself to stop them making progress through it. Which I can narrate with the best of them... but what I'm stuck for is how, in play, the PCs solve the manse. Like, it can be, roll (Perception+Occult) with a good Stunt from the players and a good description from me... but I'd prefer a real puzzle that they actually have to work out so that it feels more like they're defeating the defenses of a powerful, mystic building rather than rolling dice against a static difficulty. But I'm stuck on how to actually play that out. I'm not <i>against </i>the PCs straight-up powering their way through these puzzles with an Excellency, but I'm asking for help in making that <i>interesting </i>to play through (which might be some unique and novel thing, or it might be really basic Storytelling Advice).<br /> <br /> So... dear Exalted forum:<br /> <br /> Give me your riddles.<br /> Give me your puzzles.<br /> Give me your ideas from dungeons past.<br /> Favourite Zelda levels.<br /> Take a scene from Saw and set it up as something you could actually play through in Exalted.<br /> <br /> No criticism too harsh, no advice to obvious. I've got five days and 21 hours to think of some plot that doesn't suck. Help a brother out.<br /> <br /> What would be great, is something like <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1121_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1121\" data-vbnamecard=\"1121\">DrLoveMonkey</a>'s <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1395197-adventure-ho\">Adventure Ho!</a> for attacking The House of Black Waters. But any cool puzzles or challenges you have given players, or played through as a player, for any game would be neat inspiration. (And whatever I don't use next week can be used further down the line/might help someone else.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 10-04-2020, 05:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-04T15:45:15-07:00","id":1416776,"title":"","content":"How about a liquid that fills up the place, imposing penalties on the players? If they don't find a way to escape or an air pocket, they'll drown. The liquid is specially treated, so even if they have charms for underwater living, they have a magically imposed penalty. Meanwhile, the attack golems are now deployed. They gain bonuses in water, are invisible in liquid, and are deadly enough.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-04T15:53:59-07:00","id":1416778,"title":"","content":"One neat possibility is that, when your players leap over the garden paths and kick down the front doors of The House of Black Waters, they find a normal, unassuming Imperial residence, with the typical frightened servants and haughty, offended hosts. If the player characters burst in arms blazing then there'll probably be some initial fight, but it's also possible that they leap in and catch a group of five young Iselsi Dynasts and their hangers-on about to leave, and the youngsters run deeper into the manse frightened out of their minds.<br /> <br /> The first puzzle for your players, of course, is finding the 'real' House of Black Waters beneath the banal disguise. Maybe one player gets tired with looking for secret passageways and just blasts through some floorboards only to fall into a swiftly moving underground river that sweeps him into a dark oubliette he's got to bust out of. There could be similar traps and stuff designed to target people who just start ripping through things rather than search for the hidden entrances or what-have-you.<br /> <br /> I'd play up the cliches of Dynastic residences, with a big pagoda palace building hiding a secret fortress of stone and water beneath it. I'd have their be lots of hidden chute-like traps to channel invaders into perilous chambers and deadly traps deep below. Maybe there could be swift water-filled passages that flow through meshes of razor wire, all the better to maim any who get caught in the current.<br /> <br /> Also, since the House of Black Waters is where Iselsi herself is laid to rest there, her family are probably bastards enough to do something with her corpse. A reanimated corpse might be too much, but I could see there being some hyper-potent artifact that uses some of her bones or essence to deadly effect. Maybe a bow wielded by the House Elder that forms arrows out of water pulled from nearby sources, like the aforementioned underground rivers, pretty-looking fountains, her foe's blood, etc.<br /> <br /> Do you know what your players' plans will be?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11619-kymmetheseventh","name":"KymmetheSeventh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11619_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-04T22:54:02-07:00","id":1416798,"title":"","content":"Actual riddles are going to be very hard here, and need to be crafted in very particular ways.<br /> <br /> Mainly because a lot of people aren't good at riddles, and even people who are great at them can often just get stuck with a little mental hitch.<br /> <br /> Like &quot;I have cities, but no houses, mountains but no trees, lakes, rivers and oceans, but no fish. What am I? Speak my name and you shall have me.&quot; the answer there being a map, which would be very helpful. If nobody gets that after 5 minutes of guessing and they're just stumped, and they NEED the map to progress, then session over, or you just have to give them the answer, and that's no fun either because then they could just give up all the time and have to get it to proceed.<br /> <br /> So any real life riddles should be treated like pass-fail checks in the game. If it's 100% required, you have to let them fail and then continue, or pass, but with a penalty. The only time true failure should be a thing is when they've failed like 6 out of the total 7 challenges, and they're sitting there with no motes, willpower, or health levels left, and decide to press on anyway, even knowing the house elder and 3 exalted bodyguards are waiting in the next room.<br /> <br /> <br /> That being said I'll think of some stuff to post tomorrow if I can find the time to write it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-04T23:05:38-07:00","id":1416800,"title":"","content":"That riddle doesn't exactly work, because some maps *do* have houses on them. And it won't be out of place to have maps talking about fish swarms and migration patterns. So doing riddles has a problem because there is so much context required.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-04T23:18:40-07:00","id":1416802,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1416764-need-help-with-designing-manse-defenses?p=1416800#post1416800\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That riddle doesn't exactly work, because some maps *do* have houses on them. And it won't be out of place to have maps talking about fish swarms and migration patterns. So doing riddles has a problem because there is so much context required.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, basically all riddles have that problem, they're not logic puzzles that can be solved with a logic truth table. Most of them specifically require a logical leap, or kind of poetic inference. The Hobbit has some pretty good riddles <a href=\"http://tolkien.cro.net/talesong/riddles.html\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, and basically none of them are incontrovertibly true.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-04T23:34:20-07:00","id":1416804,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1416764-need-help-with-designing-manse-defenses?p=1416802#post1416802\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, basically all riddles have that problem, they're not logic puzzles that can be solved with a logic truth table. Most of them specifically require a logical leap, or kind of poetic inference. The Hobbit has some pretty good riddles <a href=\"http://tolkien.cro.net/talesong/riddles.html\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, and basically none of them are incontrovertibly true.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yup.<br /> <br /> I can already think of several issues. Like, say, someone not familiar with chinese culture may not be familiar with riddles involving chopsticks.<br /> <br /> edit: That teeth one is wrong. My gums are pink. Not red.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-04T23:42:46-07:00","id":1416805,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1416764-need-help-with-designing-manse-defenses?p=1416804#post1416804\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That teeth one is wrong. My gums are pink. Not red.</div> </div> </div> </div>And as Gollum immediately points out after getting the right answer &quot;We only has nine&quot; so even he had to make a leap for that there. Also most people with a full set have 32 not 30. Also making the leap of horses champing and stamping to teeth chewing is not what I would call obvious.<br /> <br /> These are the kinds of thing that get a group held up for a half hour.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-05T03:24:00-07:00","id":1416832,"title":"","content":"Traps are good. I like traps. I have a DnD folder full of traps. <br /> <br /> Puzzles are good. I like puzzles. I have a DnD folder full of puzzles. <br /> <br /> I don't have any Exalted folders full of those things because Excellencies and Charms shatter them like glass. And Int 5 Wis 5 Lore 5 Investigation 5 Twilight is literally a once in a millenium super genius. They figure out the puzzle. They solve 4d rubix cubes for fun, before breakfast. I play a this character and I have more than 10 Craft skills at rank 5 and I have Shattering Grasp, Words as Workshop Method, and Vice Miracle Technique. There just isn't a puzzle that he can't solve or disassemble unless it was made 2000 years ago by a different Twilight. <br /> <br /> Traps? Athletics and Resistance obliterate these. There's very little a superhuman muscle machine can be challenged by. The Str 5 Stm 5 Ath 5 Zenith can hold up the collapsing ceiling. The Night caste sees the tripwire in the pitch black darkness. Et cetera, et cetera. <br /> <br /> That said, if you wanna screw with them, i might have a few Diceless puzzles. <br /> <br /> The 5 Potions: pretty straitforward. There are 5 potions on the table, different bottles sizes, colors, etc. They each do something and the only way through a door is to drink the right one. There's no clue or way to discern which it is. Give out 2 boons and 2 banes. Drink up!<br /> <br /> Blood Price: you wanna pass, you gotta pay the toll. Its blood. Your blood. Half your health in blood. No cheating. Get to it. <br /> <br /> The Missing Piece: there's a mural of a famous scene on the wall, something from Exalted's Shakespeare or Waterloo or whatever. However, a major detail is missing (i.e. Romeo's knife in Juliet). You have to find it in a room full of junk, Last Crusade style. The catch is its a trap and the real key is a piece of the junk. <br /> <br /> The Wire Trick: there's a black tripwire in the hallway. About a foot after that, there's another wire camouflaged like the floor. Then 2 feet after that there's an invisble wire that's tied to the real trap. Gotcha. <br /> <br /> The upside down room: its about a 100 feet to the ceiling. Theres a door high up, that touches the ceiling. How will you get there? Surprise, gravity is reversed in this room. Hope you have a way to mitigate the fall. <br /> <br /> Sharks: just a bunch of sharks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please be warned: this is not champagne, this is most likely a duck.<br /> -<i>Chausse</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><i>Message me for Japanese translations.</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","name":"Sorcerous Overlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-05T03:27:54-07:00","id":1416833,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1416764-need-help-with-designing-manse-defenses?p=1416832#post1416832\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Traps are good. I like traps. I have a DnD folder full of traps.<br /> <br /> Puzzles are good. I like puzzles. I have a DnD folder full of puzzles.<br /> <br /> I don't have any Exalted folders full of those things because Excellencies and Charms shatter them like glass. And Int 5 Wis 5 Lore 5 Investigation 5 Twilight is literally a once in a millenium super genius. They figure out the puzzle. They solve 4d rubix cubes for fun, before breakfast. I play a this character and I have more than 10 Craft skills at rank 5 and I have Shattering Grasp, Words as Workshop Method, and Vice Miracle Technique. There just isn't a puzzle that he can't solve or disassemble unless it was made 2000 years ago by a different Twilight.<br /> <br /> Traps? Athletics and Resistance obliterate these. There's very little a superhuman muscle machine can be challenged by. The Str 5 Stm 5 Ath 5 Zenith can hold up the collapsing ceiling. The Night caste sees the tripwire in the pitch black darkness. Et cetera, et cetera.<br /> <br /> That said, if you wanna screw with them, i might have a few Diceless puzzles.<br /> <br /> The 5 Potions: pretty straitforward. There are 5 potions on the table, different bottles sizes, colors, etc. They each do something and the only way through a door is to drink the right one. There's no clue or way to discern which it is. Give out 2 boons and 2 banes. Drink up!<br /> <br /> Blood Price: you wanna pass, you gotta pay the toll. Its blood. Your blood. Half your health in blood. No cheating. Get to it.<br /> <br /> The Missing Piece: there's a mural of a famous scene on the wall, something from Exalted's Shakespeare or Waterloo or whatever. However, a major detail is missing (i.e. Romeo's knife in Juliet). You have to find it in a room full of junk, Last Crusade style. The catch is its a trap and the real key is a piece of the junk.<br /> <br /> The Wire Trick: there's a black tripwire in the hallway. About a foot after that, there's another wire camouflaged like the floor. Then 2 feet after that there's an invisble wire that's tied to the real trap. Gotcha.<br /> <br /> The upside down room: its about a 100 feet to the ceiling. Theres a door high up, that touches the ceiling. How will you get there? Surprise, gravity is reversed in this room. Hope you have a way to mitigate the fall.<br /> <br /> Sharks: just a bunch of sharks.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can think of ways to punch through these. 5 potions: Alchemical touchstones can determine what they are. Specialized charms act like spectrography, letting you figure out what each one is. Difficulty 5 to figure out from smell alone. Poof. Done. Blood Price? Get a twilight doctor, Sesseljae, or just plain ass body mending meditation after the thing. The Missing Piece, Wire Trick, can be mitigated with charms that boost intelligence, perception, and knowledge. Upside Down room has to deal with flying spells or just plain ass running up and holding down a rope.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-05T03:51:09-07:00","id":1416834,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1416764-need-help-with-designing-manse-defenses?p=1416833#post1416833\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can think of ways to punch through these. 5 potions: Alchemical touchstones can determine what they are. Specialized charms act like spectrography, letting you figure out what each one is. Difficulty 5 to figure out from smell alone. Poof. Done. Blood Price? Get a twilight doctor, Sesseljae, or just plain ass body mending meditation after the thing. The Missing Piece, Wire Trick, can be mitigated with charms that boost intelligence, perception, and knowledge. Upside Down room has to deal with flying spells or just plain ass running up and holding down a rope.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, but:<br /> <br /> 1. This isn't a hypothetical &quot;could the Exalted beat it&quot;: It's a real game with actual characters. They don't have specialized spectography charms or alchemical touchstones, and if it comes to a straight &quot;Difficulty 5 Perception roll&quot; they're only throwing 13 dice at it... that could fail.<br /> <br /> 2. It's a Dragon-Blooded game.<br /> <br /> And I'm not opposed to punching through a puzzle, or cheating it with Charms: that's the point of being a mighty Exalted hero. I just need a way to keep things interesting.<br /> <br /> Like, there's nothing wrong with just shrugging off deadly poison by spending 6m on an Excellency. Because then they can start the next combat 6m down. I just don't want to do that over and over and over and over and over again for three hours. Or, if I'm going to do it, I could use some wicked cool descriptions from y'all that I can read to the players. Or awesome rewards to break up the monotony.<br /> <br /> So... don't worry about lowballing it. Things can always be scaled up or scaled down as appropriate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-05T03:53:16-07:00","id":1416835,"title":"","content":"With respect, you treated these as if it was possible to plan for them ahead of time and build characters to match, whereas John is going into it with real players. <br /> <br /> The upside down room is there to check that you have a solution. Not that its impossible. <br /> <br /> The tripwire trick is to get you paranoid. How many more fakeouts are there? <br /> <br /> The blood price is there to screw you over. Do you travel with someone deeply invested in Medicine? Because its going to take specifically Body Sculpting Essence Method to heal you instantly. You have resistance healing charms? Cool. Those aren't free. Paying motes and willpower is still the trap working. <br /> <br /> The potion puzzle you failed. First, I cant find &quot;alchemical touchstones&quot; anywhere. Not sure what charms you think identify potions either, and you pulled the Diff 5 out of thin air. Not only that, i straight up said they can't be figured out by observation. Pure ST bullshit? Yes. But you enter a manse as a hostile foe woth no prep, thats what you get. Plus even if they had unique smell, (Which they don't) what does a key smell like? You don't know. <br /> <br /> You're also taking the Missing Piece on assumption that the answer is distinguishable from the junk by investigation. Did it occur to you that &quot;code&quot; changes randomly every day, and the answer is found on the other side? Because paranoid sorcerers would do that kind of shit. Its not a matter of what junk doesnt belong, its what junk am i looking for? I really want to know what your Investigation roll to realize that is gonna look like. <br /> <br /> These are ideas for an ST to play with, not for you to hypothetically solve with your 1337 google-fu","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please be warned: this is not champagne, this is most likely a duck.<br /> -<i>Chausse</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><i>Message me for Japanese translations.</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","name":"Sorcerous Overlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-05T03:57:41-07:00","id":1416837,"title":"","content":"That's nice.<br /> <br /> So.... Where are the stats for the PCs?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-05T04:25:30-07:00","id":1416839,"title":"","content":"More of a set-piece rather than something helpful towards your maze idea (sorry), but as its Iselsi with their masks within masks, personas within personas schtick, my mind wandered to something like the players being steered into a secret room under the influence of an N/A hearthstone or the like where they\u2019re challenged one at a time by \u2018alternative\u2019 versions of themselves, personas they might have previously aspired to if events had played out differently and that they have to \u2018give up\u2019/slay in order to recognise the truth about themselves and progess into the next chamber.<br /> <br /> So, Ganan is socially challenged by the perfect Cynis Dynast he\u2019s never been able to be, Reya is forced to confront a version of herself who rules over Dovak with Tinkara (?) and the like. The other characters can help by making their own relevant rolls in the background maybe (role-played as shouting encouragement, \u2018Remember who you are\u2019 type stuff), adding a bonus success to the main event if they beat a set difficulty.<br /> <br /> Players beat it, but are drained heading into the final big showdown with the Manse's big guns.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24647-moss-reynholm","name":"Moss Reynholm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24647_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-05T04:41:10-07:00","id":1416842,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar531_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"531\" data-vbnamecard=\"531\">JohnDoe244</a> So what are the stats of your DB players? Did I miss a stat block somewhere?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-05T06:08:20-07:00","id":1416849,"title":"","content":"Oh one more thing, is this something that they have to do without planning, or can they spend a session gathering info and preparing for the infiltration? <br /> <br /> It feels like things should be extremely difficult to just go in blind with no plan trying to break into the inner sanctum of the fortress HQ of one of the most advanced counter-intelligence organizations in the world. It\u2019s like Mission Impossible without the \u201cdun-dun-dun-dah-dah-dah-dun first unger uses the phone company credentials we stole to infiltrate the network room and set up an interrupting router bypass, then we head in to the low security employee parking and head for the ventilation shaft, by then our special delivery sleeping poison should be in the director\u2019s lunch...\u201d","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-05T06:37:07-07:00","id":1416853,"title":"","content":"13 dice on difficulty 5 is roughly an 80% chance for success, blowing a WP would make it a 90%.<br /> <br /> I do not recommend binary win/loss rolls that would effectively halt the stories. If such a thing is a case, let them possibly come back and retry the roll after reading a local library, or maybe a local legend somehow references the riddle in a way.<br /> <br /> As for traps, I went over some possibilities in my <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1407650-shantytown-of-the-awesome-building-and-manse-3e-homebrew\">manse homebrew</a>. Or just anything from La-Mulana, that'll make people's brains turn into pretzels.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Read my shit at my <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/271207-sandact6-homebrew-topic\" target=\"_blank\">homebrew</a> topic, 2.5e and 3e material!<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1263020-alchemicals-2-0-3e-conversion-charm-design-request\" target=\"_blank\">Play Alchemical's in 3e now</a>, you're welcome.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1183-sandact6","name":"Sandact6","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1183_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-05T06:55:05-07:00","id":1416855,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1416764-need-help-with-designing-manse-defenses?p=1416849#post1416849\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh one more thing, is this something that they have to do without planning, or can they spend a session gathering info and preparing for the infiltration? <br /> <br /> It feels like things should be extremely difficult to just go in blind with no plan trying to break into the inner sanctum of the fortress HQ of one of the most advanced counter-intelligence organizations in the world. It\u2019s like Mission Impossible without the \u201cdun-dun-dun-dah-dah-dah-dun first unger uses the phone company credentials we stole to infiltrate the network room and set up an interrupting router bypass, then we head in to the low security employee parking and head for the ventilation shaft, by then our special delivery sleeping poison should be in the director\u2019s lunch...\u201d</div> </div> </div> </div>There's no reason why they couldn't plan. I have no problem with them busting in unprepared and having to run away, if it makes for good drama rather than a railroady f-u.<br /> <br /> But my instinct is they won't plan.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sandact6</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1416764-need-help-with-designing-manse-defenses?p=1416853#post1416853\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">13 dice on difficulty 5 is roughly an 80% chance for success, blowing a WP would make it a 90%.<br /> <br /> I do not recommend binary win/loss rolls that would effectively halt the stories. If such a thing is a case, let them possibly come back and retry the roll after reading a local library, or maybe a local legend somehow references the riddle in a way.<br /> <br /> As for traps, I went over some possibilities in my <a href=\"http://&quot;&#91;url\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1407650-shantytown-of-the-awesome-building-and-manse-3e-homebrew&quot;]manse</a> homebrew[/URL]. Or just anything from La-Mulana, that'll make people's brains turn into pretzels.</div> </div> </div> </div>This isn't really part of the story. It's just something the players said they wanted to do off the cuff. Like last session they said they wanted to fight a Warstrider so I shoehorned it in. We just roll the mics and whatever happens happens (ridiculous debauchery, stuff not made for children's ears).<br /> <br /> But definitely some good stuff in your homebrew there to steal.<br /> <br /> (90% chance of brute force success is fine. They have like 2WP at the moment from not sleeping. If they want to blow 6m and 1WP to skip a puzzle that suits me to the ground. And generally it's pretty easy to &quot;no but&quot; these kinds of things -- Can't identify the potion? Better drink 'em all. Heck, my PCs probably would drink them all as Plan A.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moss Reynholm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1416764-need-help-with-designing-manse-defenses?p=1416839#post1416839\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">More of a set-piece rather than something helpful towards your maze idea (sorry), but as its Iselsi with their masks within masks, personas within personas schtick, my mind wandered to something like the players being steered into a secret room under the influence of an N/A hearthstone or the like where they\u2019re challenged one at a time by \u2018alternative\u2019 versions of themselves, personas they might have previously aspired to if events had played out differently and that they have to \u2018give up\u2019/slay in order to recognise the truth about themselves and progess into the next chamber.<br /> <br /> So, Ganan is socially challenged by the perfect Cynis Dynast he\u2019s never been able to be, Reya is forced to confront a version of herself who rules over Dovak with Tinkara (?) and the like. The other characters can help by making their own relevant rolls in the background maybe (role-played as shouting encouragement, \u2018Remember who you are\u2019 type stuff), adding a bonus success to the main event if they beat a set difficulty.<br /> <br /> Players beat it, but are drained heading into the final big showdown with the Manse's big guns.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh that's f***ing solid gold.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KymmetheSeventh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1416764-need-help-with-designing-manse-defenses?p=1416778#post1416778\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One neat possibility is that, when your players leap over the garden paths and kick down the front doors of The House of Black Waters, they find a normal, unassuming Imperial residence, with the typical frightened servants and haughty, offended hosts. If the player characters burst in arms blazing then there'll probably be some initial fight, but it's also possible that they leap in and catch a group of five young Iselsi Dynasts and their hangers-on about to leave, and the youngsters run deeper into the manse frightened out of their minds.</div> </div> </div> </div>Appropriated.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Maybe one player gets tired with looking for secret passageways and just blasts through some floorboards only to fall into a swiftly moving underground river that sweeps him into a dark oubliette he's got to bust out of. </div> </div> </div>It's like you know my players.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, since the House of Black Waters is where Iselsi herself is laid to rest there, her family are probably bastards enough to do something with her corpse. A reanimated corpse might be too much, but I could see there being some hyper-potent artifact that uses some of her bones or essence to deadly effect. </div> </div> </div>I like the idea of Iselsi turning in her grave actually. Let me work on that. Hmm...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Do you know what your players' plans will be? </div> </div> </div>Honestly? I'll be surprised if they don't just try setting the damn thing on fire.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1416764-need-help-with-designing-manse-defenses?p=1416837#post1416837\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's nice.<br /> <br /> So.... Where are the stats for the PCs?</div> </div> </div> </div>Eeeeehhhhh.<br /> <br /> I mean, I can link 'em. But that's not really the help I need.<br /> <br /> Scaling difficulties up and down or going &quot;man that's cool, but it doesn't fit my players&quot; is something I'm perfectly capable of doing. I don't need you to tailor this to my PCs or Dragon-Blooded (or even to 3E). I need coolness. I need ideas. I need a &quot;fair&quot; challenge that I will then skew in favour of the PCs as I see fit.<br /> <br /> But if you really want the stats <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12952\" data-vbnamecard=\"12952\">Accelerator</a>:<br /> <br /> PC1<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Mnemon Alinos Danireya \u2013 A hero<br /> Reya is the eldest daughter of Mnemon Alinos and her heir apparent, also being technically the Satrap of Dovak. Reya leaves behind the power-base she has meticulously built in the Threshold of the Realm to return to the Realm\u2019s heart, the Blessed Isle, where she is but a small fish in a much larger pond. A powerful sorceress and burgeoning politico, she has also claimed a powerful artifact from House Ragara.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Hoping she can use the political connections made in her youth to avert the impending Civil War, Reya answers her Matriarch\u2019s call to war with grim-faced duty. Reya is 13 weeks pregnant with her third child.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Mnemon Alinos Danireya<br /> <br /> Air Aspect<br /> Heptagram<br /> Aspiring Matriarch<br /> <br /> Session 50 \u2013 Reya (130XP 104DX, 127/103 spent; 9GP 11SP)<br /> <br /> Strength 2<br /> Dexterity 3<br /> Stamina 2<br /> <br /> Charisma 2<br /> Manipulation 5 (16DX)<br /> Appearance 5<br /> <br /> Perception 3<br /> Intelligence 3<br /> Wits 3<br /> <br /> Air Aspect Abilities (and Specialties) (6 BP)<br /> <br /> Linguistics 5<br /> Lore: Heptagram education 5 (Mathematics)<br /> <br /> Occult 5 (The Burning Name)<br /> <br /> Stealth 0<br /> <br /> Thrown 0<br /> <br /> Favored Abilities (7BP)<br /> <br /> Craft: Weapons 2 (Axes) (1DX)<br /> <br /> Integrity 5<br /> <br /> Performance 3 (Singing)<br /> <br /> Presence 5 (Imperious Matriarch, 3XP)<br /> Socialize 5 (High Society)<br /> <br /> Other