ivider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 10-05-2020, 06:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-05T07:24:44-07:00","id":1416858,"title":"","content":"A question. What your goal foe them? Is the pc supposed to win no matter what, or is there a storyline for them to get captured?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-05T07:49:58-07:00","id":1416859,"title":"","content":"Wait are they just heading there to destroy it? Because that changes things a whole lot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-05T12:32:33-07:00","id":1416888,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KymmetheSeventh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1416764-need-help-with-designing-manse-defenses?p=1416778#post1416778\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The first puzzle for your players, of course, is finding the 'real' House of Black Waters beneath the banal disguise. Maybe one player gets tired with looking for secret passageways and just blasts through some floorboards only to fall into a swiftly moving underground river that sweeps him into a dark oubliette he's got to bust out of. There could be similar traps and stuff designed to target people who just start ripping through things rather than search for the hidden entrances or what-have-you.<br /> <br /> I'd play up the cliches of Dynastic residences, with a big pagoda palace building hiding a secret fortress of stone and water beneath it. I'd have their be lots of hidden chute-like traps to channel invaders into perilous chambers and deadly traps deep below. Maybe there could be swift water-filled passages that flow through meshes of razor wire, all the better to maim any who get caught in the current.</div> </div> </div> </div>I really like that, but why razor wire when you can have coral?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KymmetheSeventh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1416764-need-help-with-designing-manse-defenses?p=1416778#post1416778\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, since the House of Black Waters is where Iselsi herself is laid to rest there, her family are probably bastards enough to do something with her corpse. A reanimated corpse might be too much, but I could see there being some hyper-potent artifact that uses some of her bones or essence to deadly effect. Maybe a bow wielded by the House Elder that forms arrows out of water pulled from nearby sources, like the aforementioned underground rivers, pretty-looking fountains, her foe's blood, etc.<br /> <br /> Do you know what your players' plans will be?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, one could have the underground &quot;true manse&quot; as an essence-infused coral reef, living, breathing, subtly changing in architecture, with an arcane ecosystem of mundane &amp; supernatural inhabitants, the water &amp; essence of neighboring streams, lakes &amp; falls flowing, mixing and bringing the remnants of lost, drowned things &amp; people to rest placidly in its depths, in the siren-like embrace of Iselsi's singing (hungry) ghost, for example.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 10-05-2020, 03:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-05T15:13:28-07:00","id":1416903,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1416764-need-help-with-designing-manse-defenses?p=1416858#post1416858\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A question. What your goal foe them? Is the pc supposed to win no matter what, or is there a storyline for them to get captured?</div> </div> </div> </div>The goal is to fill a fun three hours.<br /> <br /> Uh... let's see.<br /> <br /> Okay. Two weeks ago, P2 is flicking through Arms and says &quot;Man warstriders are cool -- look at this horse one&quot;. And P1 goes, &quot;Warstriders suck, I think we'd actually be weaker if we had one&quot;. Then P3 says, &quot;well the only way to settle this is with a Warstrider fight!&quot;*<br /> <br /> Plotwise, the characters were in the middle of flying across the length of the Blessed Isle, having recruited Berit to take command of their army in the Realm civil war. Nothing we were doing had anything to do with Warstriders. There was no wider plot point about Warstriders. Warstriders have nothing to do with traveling across the Blessed Isle. But we did this: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1341506-dynasty-of-dovak-campaign-notes-and-play-report?p=1416731#post1416731\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...31#post1416731</a> (Take a Nephwrack, give it all of the Cathedral of Sublime Annihilation's Resonant Evocations, you got yourself a Session.)<br /> <br /> The plot point, was me shoehorning in &quot;Sidereals might be responsible for all your problems&quot;. But the main focus of the session was based on a throwaway comment the week before.<br /> <br /> Last week, P2 is thumbing through WFHW and he says to me, &quot;man we really should deal with those Iselsi a-holes&quot;. And here we are.<br /> <br /> It doesn't really matter if they win or lose. So long as they don't die. Normally, I don't need help planning sessions. But normally we finish play by 2200 on Saturday and I have nine hours of potential plot ready by 0800 Sunday. But this is kicking my ass. I'm wracking my brain, but nothing I can think of seems fun. This thread has been a great help. I think I can fill a session with what I've got. (But I'm also going to need traps for the Imperial Manse in ~14 sessions time and this is a gold mine, so keep the idea-juice flowing.)<br /> <br /> If they lose, they need to be taken prisoner so they can break out or get rescued. Or be forced to run away. So it's probably cleaner if they win. But winning isn't required: they've had their asses kicked before (one session finished with the PCs unconscious, disarmed, hogtied, and about to be eaten -- the next session was one of my favourites so far). I've got plot arcs, but I don't plan out specific sessions more than a week in advance, because PCs do crazy, unexpected things. There's no specific storyline for them getting captured. There's no specific storyline for if they win. I'll make it up as we go along.<br /> <br /> *If anyone was wondering, the consensus is that Warstriders are AMAZING and we need three.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1416764-need-help-with-designing-manse-defenses?p=1416859#post1416859\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wait are they just heading there to destroy it? Because that changes things a whole lot.</div> </div> </div> </div>They're heading there, ostensibly, to wipe out House Iselsi. Obviously, I'm not just going to let them just set fire to the manse. It's a manse. Obviously the players know that this won't wipe out House Iselsi, but they see it as a fun way to make an exciting new enemy... and there's no reason for the characters to suspect that House Iselsi is anything more than it seems.<br /> <br /> IC, the PCs work for Mnemon. Mnemon will want to get the PCs out from under her feet now that they've successfully fetched her tartan paint and elbow grease. Mnemon hates House Iselsi. It's not a stretch.<br /> <br /> They're attacking the manse. They know they needa Greater Hearthstone to power their Warstrider once it's repaired, so I assume they'll want to capture the manse rather than destroy it outright. But... they do like destroying things outright.<br /> <br /> I can always have Mnemon tell them NOT to destroy the manse.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 10-05-2020, 06:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-05T17:56:34-07:00","id":1416916,"title":"","content":"How about this, John Doe. I'm not quite sure how to run it, but maybe have the manse defenses also be their verification protocols, as befits the crime-syndicate and ninja theme of Iselsi? Fail and you get thrown out or hurt. Succeed and you can go deeper into the manse. Succeed really well? You get extra bonuses. This is the headquarters of the Iselsi.<br /> <br /> You can probably gain access to their armoury, or important documentation, or maybe even a secret mini-shapeshifting warstrider in their headquarters meant for emergencies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-05T18:12:31-07:00","id":1416920,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1416764-need-help-with-designing-manse-defenses?p=1416903#post1416903\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The goal is to fill a fun three hours.<br /> <br /> Uh... let's see.<br /> <br /> Okay. Two weeks ago, P2 is flicking through Arms and says &quot;Man warstriders are cool -- look at this horse one&quot;. And P1 goes, &quot;Warstriders suck, I think we'd actually be weaker if we had one&quot;. Then P3 says, &quot;well the only way to settle this is with a Warstrider fight!&quot;*<br /> <br /> Plotwise, the characters were in the middle of flying across the length of the Blessed Isle, having recruited Berit to take command of their army in the Realm civil war. Nothing we were doing had anything to do with Warstriders. There was no wider plot point about Warstriders. Warstriders have nothing to do with traveling across the Blessed Isle. But we did this: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1341506-dynasty-of-dovak-campaign-notes-and-play-report?p=1416731#post1416731\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...31#post1416731</a> (Take a Nephwrack, give it all of the Cathedral of Sublime Annihilation's Resonant Evocations, you got yourself a Session.)<br /> <br /> The plot point, was me shoehorning in &quot;Sidereals might be responsible for all your problems&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>In a quite stealthy yet deadpan manner, might be said. Good one that bit with Danireya.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1416764-need-help-with-designing-manse-defenses?p=1416903#post1416903\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Last week, P2 is thumbing through WFHW and he says to me, &quot;man we really should deal with those Iselsi a-holes&quot;. And here we are.<br /> <br /> It doesn't really matter if they win or lose. So long as they don't die. Normally, I don't need help planning sessions. But normally we finish play by 2200 on Saturday and I have nine hours of potential plot ready by 0800 Sunday. But this is kicking my ass. I'm wracking my brain, but nothing I can think of seems fun. This thread has been a great help. I think I can fill a session with what I've got. (But I'm also going to need traps for the Imperial Manse in ~14 sessions time and this is a gold mine, so keep the idea-juice flowing.)<br /> <br /> If they lose, they need to be taken prisoner so they can break out or get rescued. Or be forced to run away. So it's probably cleaner if they win. But winning isn't required: they've had their asses kicked before (one session finished with the PCs unconscious, disarmed, hogtied, and about to be eaten -- the next session was one of my favourites so far). I've got plot arcs, but I don't plan out specific sessions more than a week in advance, because PCs do crazy, unexpected things. There's no specific storyline for them getting captured. There's no specific storyline for if they win. I'll make it up as we go along.<br /> <br /> *If anyone was wondering, the consensus is that Warstriders are AMAZING and we need three.<br /> <br /> <br /> They're heading there, ostensibly, to wipe out House Iselsi. Obviously, I'm not just going to let them just set fire to the manse. It's a manse. Obviously the players know that this won't wipe out House Iselsi, but they see it as a fun way to make an exciting new enemy... and there's no reason for the characters to suspect that House Iselsi is anything more than it seems.<br /> <br /> IC, the PCs work for Mnemon. Mnemon will want to get the PCs out from under her feet now that they've successfully fetched her tartan paint and elbow grease. Mnemon hates House Iselsi. It's not a stretch.<br /> <br /> They're attacking the manse. They know they need a Greater Hearthstone to power their Warstrider once it's repaired, so I assume they'll want to capture the manse rather than destroy it outright. But... they do like destroying things outright.<br /> <br /> I can always have Mnemon tell them NOT to destroy the manse.</div> </div> </div> </div>For extra complications, what if the Sesus, the <b>other </b>house with infamous spymasters, had one or more scions secretly watching the manse, just waiting for some other house or alliance to make first move? What side will they take - attackers, defenders, kill-'em-all - completely open to whatever suits you when the time comes, to provide either complication or life-saving distraction.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-05T22:32:15-07:00","id":1416946,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1416764-need-help-with-designing-manse-defenses?p=1416903#post1416903\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They're heading there, ostensibly, to wipe out House Iselsi. Obviously, I'm not just going to let them just set fire to the manse. It's a manse. Obviously the players know that this won't wipe out House Iselsi, but they see it as a fun way to make an exciting new enemy... and there's no reason for the characters to suspect that House Iselsi is anything more than it seems.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah true, Iselsi isn't exactly making its power known. Just busting into the HQ of a great house with your party to take them out by punching them is throwing me a bit of a loop, but I can see it working in a particular style of game.<br /> <br /> Okay, so the House of Black Water. How do you get black water? Well either the water itself has to be really murky, or inked somehow, or it needs to be really deep, or in a really dark place. So let's mix those last two here.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> The demense which was to become the House of Black Waters was a massive rocky outcropping, cleft nearly in two, in the Incas Valley. In the middle of this crevasse lay a lake, a lake so deep and so dark that many still affirm that it has truly no bottom at all. This opinion is reenforced by the unique manse that caps it. Starting at the shore, there is a small cluster of buildings that house minor guards, some groundskeeping staff, and unwanted-guest rooms.<br /> <br /> Coming out into the lake from this small village is bridge, long, wide, and made of immaculately fitted wood. Thousands of planks long, and on each side flanked by rows of dim lanterns it represents the only terrestrial path to the House of Black Waters. Either constructed on a foundation deep in the dark lake, or else entirely floating on the surface of the water, rises a mansion of imperial stature and proportion.<br /> <br /> The water-level square on the perimeter of the manse is covered with greenery, gardens, lawns, and gazebos. Many of which are connected to their own little dock where sleek and beautiful boats are moored. The house uses them for pleasure and training out further in open water. Terraced up from this are several other levels replete with various verandas and balconies, and at the very top some high towers.<br /> <br /> This is only half of the manse, however, the mask over the face. The true depths of its character lie below the water's surface. Through hidden passages in the manse, past guards and wards, there lies the hidden heart of Iselsi. They're far too experienced to keep all of their most sensitive information there, far more of it is distributed across the globe, but in hidden vaults in the depths lie weapons, and coded information that form the dagger in the cloak.<br /> <br /> Of course the number of people in the manse who even know if the existence of those places is small indeed, and House Iselsi has spent decades of work and hundreds of talents of jade making special modifications. Much of that spent on ironwood.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Scene 1 Foyer to Elder</b><br /> <br /> This may not necessarily be the foyer, but it's whatever room the players show up at first. This is under the assumption that they get to the manse without incident. If they passed through the gatehouse area the defenses there are not enough to warrant fighting. The players burst into the manse to find nothing but fleeing servants and terrified functionaries. Some with more stern resolve have the presence of mind to surrender to this assault.<br /> <br /> One has been conditioned to offer to bring the group to the elder of the house in exchange for her life, which she will attempt to bargain for with a roll of 8 dice if she's not taken on her offer. This is not a lie, or a witting plant, it's a legitimate offer, she simply has had her intimacies manipulated to value her life more than the household she serves, and given false information about where the elder is. She leads them deeper into the manse, through the narrow wood-paneled servant backways, quieting those she comes across as part of the deal.<br /> <br /> She says that the elder is behind one final door, one which is made of an ironwood laminant and she knows it's locked. A Dex + Larceny roll of difficulty 4, or a Feat of Demolition Strength 5 Difficulty 8 will also open it.<br /> <br /> Behind the door sits the figure of the house elder. In reality this is a Sculpted Seafoam Eidolon, and a trap. She nods to the players and invites them in to discuss terms of surrender, and once everyone is safely inside the room hits a lever with her foot. This causes the whole room to disconnect from the superstructure of the manse and plummet onto a hard stone floor two range bands down. Appropriate athletics rolls and stunts can reduce this damage.<br /> <br /> Even if they manage to spot the trap and avoid it, they know they have not found their elder, and throughout the manse above/around them they here the bustling of movement.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Scene 2 Getting Out From Behind the Mask</b><br /> <br /> It's become obvious at this point that not all here will be as it seems, and nobody can be trusted. Even worse, if the players attempt to go back the way they came, they find that the walls have shifted, the path no longer exists. Attempting to smash through the wall where once there was a door proves difficult, as just under the surface of any wood panel is yet more ironwood, same difficulty to smash through as the door, and doing so isn't much help as the hallway that was there now goes perpendicular to the way it was.<br /> <br /> Navigating out of this maze is either an extended Perception + Investigation roll, difficulty 3, goal number 10, terminus 3 task, or three consecutive wall bashes must be made. Failure at either of these indicates the manse has rearranged itself and placed the characters at the start of a new maze. Freedom lets the players break back out into the public areas of the manse.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Scene 3 Apartments Down Below</b><br /> <br /> The players may now proceed to investigate the manse proper, but find only unhelpful servants just as confused as ever. At some point though they find something, either some discarded scrap of information or see somebody just in time to watch them slip into a hidden door in the wall, behind which is a long spiral staircase downward. Whatever information it is, the players are lead to believe that the real treasure is far down below.<br /> <br /> Getting down to the bottom of the public-facing manse is easy, and bashing through the floor another ironwood difficulty. Either that or a difficulty 4 Perception + Investigation roll to find a hidden passage opening.<br /> <br /> Once down there they find the structure they're in changed. Now granite stone replaces wood paneling, and darkness pervades every hallway and room. They pass some rooms with simple but comfortable living quarters, as well as some storage rooms for food, first aid supplies, and weapons. However the only way forward seems to be a deep pool of dark water on the other side of the apartment level. A difficulty 2 Perception + Investigation check reveals that indeed this way does have a lot of foot traffic.<br /> <br /> <br /> Any attempt to breach the under-manse from the outside is a difficulty 15 Strength 10+ feat of strength, and will lead the characters to a random room except the final one.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Scene 4 Teeth of the Deep</b><br /> <br /> With no other option than to press forward, the characters descend into the water, which glows faintly. Still dim enough to impose a -2 penalty on sight based actions. The pool leads deep down, for a long time, and then opening into a larger cavern. Three range bands forward is a moon pool, leading back up to the surface at the lower level. Unfortunately, they're not the only ones down here. They are ambushed as they cross by a group of 4 Benthic Knifetooth's, but that's not all. In the second round of combat a light flickers into view, glowing runes covering an armored carapace. It is a captured legendary Armored Terror. This terror has a spiritual heritage and access to the latent abilities and charms of its statline. It also blockades the moon pool exit.<br /> <br /> The players may either attempt to escape or battle the creatures, but keep in mind that under duress the characters can only stay under water for Stamina x 2 rounds before drowning. The fish are instinctively aware of this facet of prey, and often attempt grapples to keep underwater.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Scene 5 Rainbow Stairs</b><br /> <br /> The players then exit the moon pool to find themselves in front of two doors, one Red, the other Violet. The inscription above reads that essence is required to open these doors. A suitably epic feat of demolition, or a mote of essence may do the trick. Also a small riddle, &quot;Water turning hard to soft, and bread from soft to hard, this is how we go&quot; as a hint to start cold and go warm on the colour spectrum.<br /> <br /> Whichever one the characters attempt to open, they find a staircase leading down, and to another landing with another set of doors. If they picked red, this one has a red and orange door, if they picked violet a violet and blue one.<br /> <br /> Going down the same coloured door as before leads them back to the landing they first ended up on. If they progress through the correct doors in the colours of the rainbow, either backwards or forwards, they end up in a new hallway. If they didn't take the riddles advice of going cold to hot the final door breaks its hinges and flings itself towards them. Hazard of Dex + Dodge difficulty 4, damage 4B.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Scene 6 Riddle Door </b><br /> <br /> The hallway next leads curving back on itself as it slopes down, and ends in a door with a face. It stops the players and says it doesn't recognize them, but no matter, for it was designed to let clever people past. It has four riddles, which it says answering them will let them trough. Pick any four from this website.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://parade.com/947956/parade/riddles/\" target=\"_blank\">https://parade.com/947956/parade/riddles/</a><br /> <br /> He asks them one at a time, humming at their answers, but not accepting them until they confirm it is their final answer. A Read Intentions roll against his guile of 5 allows a player to see if their guess is correct, with a fail telling them that it is. Regardless when he splits open to admit them he also unleashes a cloud of noxious gas, difficulty (1 + Number of failed riddes) damage (2 + Number of failed riddles)L.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Scene 7 Nightmare Maze</b><br /> <br /> Another moon pool, and more tracks leading into it. This time though the water is murky, black even with the light of arcane magic or anima, full of some inky pollutant. The reverse side of the face door has another riddle, &quot;Mountains but no trees, rivers but no fish, cities but no people, what am I?&quot; if they guess a map correctly it produces one of the maze they are about to encounter.<br /> <br /> The pool doesn't just lead to an underwater room, but an underwater maze. An extended Perception + Survival roll of difficulty 3, goal number 10 to get through. There is no terminus, but the interval is thirty seconds and people drown after Stamina minutes under water. Having the map reduces the difficulty by 1, as do charms that allow sight without seeing.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Scene 8 The Final Battle</b><br /> <br /> At last at the end of the long chain of guarding puzzles and traps, the players face off against the house Elder, having had plenty of time and warning to prepare with her dragonblooded in the hearthroom. The players exit into another moon pool in the center of a round room. This room has all manner of devices, books, scrolls, and even some creatures in cages and tanks adorned around it. On another level, a gallery above are more treasures. Also stationed there are a pair of archers, having both Short range from the pool from above and Heavy Cover due to the granite railings.<br /> <br /> On the ground outside the pool is the House Elder and one of her best shikari fighters. They mean to end the players there. Or if they want to they can attempt to flee and escape. Successfully beating them gives them access to the hearthstone room, and many Iselsi secrets, although, of course, not all, and not even most.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Okay, that was a little janky but normally I have more time to come up with these and think about them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-05T23:30:31-07:00","id":1416950,"title":"","content":"Further thought: your characters have had a few run ins with Ragara now. Not sure of what your plans are for him, but if you're planning on using the Earth Immacualte at the manse (either fighting in the manse's defence or, more creditably, paying homage to her ancestor before she slips away to complete the deed she's been assigned. Maybe both...), maybe that Immacualte could be Moonless River \u2013 someone the PCs recognise as tagging along inconspiculously in the background amidst Ragara's entourage when they fought the warstrider/met Berit.<br /> <br /> What do they do with that information might offer some story hooks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24647,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24647-moss-reynholm","user":"Moss Reynholm","date":". 10-06-2020, 02:37 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24647-moss-reynholm","name":"Moss Reynholm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24647_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-05T23:43:37-07:00","id":1416951,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moss Reynholm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1416764-need-help-with-designing-manse-defenses?p=1416950#post1416950\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Further thought: your characters have had a few run ins with Ragara now. Not sure of what your plans are for him, but if you're planning on using the Earth Immacualte at the manse (either fighting in the manse's defence or, more creditably, paying homage to her ancestor before she slips away to complete the deed she's been assigned. Maybe both...), maybe that Immacualte could be Moonless River \u2013 someone the PCs recognise as tagging along inconspiculously in the background amidst Ragara's entourage when they fought the warstrider/met Berit.<br /> <br /> What do they do with that information might offer some story hooks.</div> </div> </div> </div>Great idea. I was thinking of using Moonless River to transition into the next plot point.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1416764-need-help-with-designing-manse-defenses?p=1416946#post1416946\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Okay, that was a little janky but normally I have more time to come up with these and think about them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Don't be modest, this is great stuff. Excellent bones, very usable material. I'm very grateful.<br /> <br /> And, you're right, it's atypical play here. The complaint from the players is that I give the Blessed Isle too much inertia, so we're butchering that particular sacred cow on the alter of &quot;Yes, and&quot;. We've not quite gone &quot;And I'll Form The Head&quot;, but we've left &quot;A Land Once Divided&quot; in the dust.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 10-06-2020, 02:46 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-06T07:50:40-07:00","id":1416994,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1416764-need-help-with-designing-manse-defenses?p=1416951#post1416951\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Great idea. I was thinking of using Moonless River to transition into the next plot point.<br /> <br /> <br /> Don't be modest, this is great stuff. Excellent bones, very usable material. I'm very grateful.<br /> <br /> And, you're right, it's atypical play here. The complaint from the players is that I give the Blessed Isle too much inertia, so we're butchering that particular sacred cow on the alter of &amp;quot;Yes, and&amp;quot;. We've not quite gone &amp;quot;And I'll Form The Head&amp;quot;, but we've left &amp;quot;A Land Once Divided&amp;quot; in the dust.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah okay, I was also having some trouble morphing an assault into a puzzle dungeon when the players don\u2019t even know there is one. A suggestion I might make is that if the players acquire knowledge of this beforehand it could make a lot smoother transition. <br /> <br /> I can see a tone of I\u2019ll Form the Head just going to punch down a great house HQ though. That kind of game doesn\u2019t care so much about the ripple of various negative consequences that would have, and how hard it would probably be, and more focuses on running around knocking out unrealistically critical lynchpin foes.<br /> <br /> Kind of like blowing up the Death Star and just assuming the empire is basically over now, when they have a massive fleet, planetary governors, and production facilities all over the galaxy still.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-13T14:48:56-07:00","id":1418097,"title":"","content":"Thinking about it more I can suggest some other things for my version of the House of Black Waters.<br /> <br /> Originally I didn't put a scene at the gatehouse because I figured the PCs would just Stormwind Rider over the lake if they're assaulting it. Then I thought that in a world with sorcerers, air elementals, flying carpets, Lunar Exalted, airships, agata, and flying whales from the Wyld, there's little chance that a major faction stronghold HQ is just defenseless from air attacks.<br /> <br /> So something like this:<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Tornadoes and Sharks</b> &lt;- WIP name, may be a better way to fuse them.<br /> <br /> If an assailant attempts to fly over the black water lake, it starts to swirl and foam beneath them, quickly sending twisting jets of water into the air. Fliers must then engage in an extended roll, using whatever stats are appropriate, for example Sail + Wits if flying an airship. The roll has a difficulty of 3, and a goal number of 10, advancement allowing the characters to move across the lake. Failure ends in them being dashed down to the water by one of the water spouts.<br /> <br /> Once in the water the characters are assaulted by a school of sharks. If the sharks are defeated the characters may either retake to the air or attempt to swim to the house, although depending on how far along the extended roll they were this may take some time. Simple sharks may also be too mundane for a water manse's watery defenses.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Suspicious Gateguard</b><br /> <br /> If the players attempt to just walk in they are stopped at the gate by a mortal with the stats of an Elite Bodyguard. He's got the following intimacies<br /> <br /> Defining Fellow Guards (Loyalty)<br /> Major House Iselsi (Loyalty)<br /> Major Husband (Love)<br /> Major Immaculate Order (Faith)<br /> Minor Things that live in the black waters (Fear)<br /> <br /> <br /> If he can be convinced that the PCs have legit business there in these times of open war then they will be let through, otherwise he assaults them with his fellow guards. He commands a size 1 battlegroup of elite bodyguards with elite drill while a sniper takes shots from an elevated position in cover. For the sniper use the stats of a horse archer with +2 bow damage representing a longbow and in heavy cover.<br /> <br /> Note that this is only really worth busting out the dice for if the players have a tendency to gleefully dunk on mortals with much more effort than is strictly necessary.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}